  "application_type_full": "Prior Approval: Larger Home Extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed extension, by reason of its excessive depth and proximity to habitable windows along the shared boundary, would result in an unacceptable loss of light and outlook and an increased sense of enclosure to the adjoining occupiers at No. 27 Grosvenor Road, causing significant harm to their living conditions. As the current proposal is materially identical to that previously refused under application PA/2026/087, and no material changes to the surrounding built environment or neighbouring properties have occurred since that assessment, the adverse impact identified remains. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies CC2 and SC7 of the Hounslow Local Plan and the objectives of the Residential Extensions Guidelines (Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD).\r\n"
  ],
